        <body>
            <div xml:id="d595">

                <pb facs="0656" n="552" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg552"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/4763</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chief of the Division of Far Eastern
                        Affairs (Hornbeck)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-03-10">March 10, 1932</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Dr. Hawkling Yen has just read me a
                    telegram received from Dr. W. W. Yen, at
                    Geneva, as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Please inform Mr. Stimson
                            substance of his talk with you made public here by me because while
                            views of member Governments of Assembly made known on open debate,
                            American view unknown to members who often in such matters were misled
                            through tendential reports of American attitude. Hope he will understand
                            my motive.”</p></quote></p>
                <closer><signed>S[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >tanley</hi>] K. H[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >ornbeck</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
